{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-107495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the principal $20$th root of unity." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5f3091f264237278f4b144b278a0fdd1e98fbbdc12ba8d800aea360a64ad1c7"} {"question" "q-107495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $z$ be a $20$th root of unity. This means that \n\n$$\n{z}^{20}=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the complex number $1$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta }.$ Notice that $|1|=1$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(1)=0.$ Hence, \n\n$$\n1={e}^{\\text{i}(0+2k\\pi )}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is an integer. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{20}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}}\\,⟹\\,z=({e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}})^{1/20}={e}^{k\\pi \\text{i}/10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe principal root corresponds to $k=1,$ and is therefore equal to ${e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/10}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5f3091f264237278f4b144b278a0fdd1e98fbbdc12ba8d800aea360a64ad1c7"} {"question" "q-107495" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "efeba78947963653518be88df3e317edf940418a7f26a0b9199e31abd8f0bf40"} {"question" "q-107495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5f3091f264237278f4b144b278a0fdd1e98fbbdc12ba8d800aea360a64ad1c7"} {"question" "q-107495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/5}"] ["math" "{e}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/10}"] ["math" "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/10}"] ["math" "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/20}"] ["math" "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/40}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5f3091f264237278f4b144b278a0fdd1e98fbbdc12ba8d800aea360a64ad1c7"} {"question" "q-107495" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/10}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5f3091f264237278f4b144b278a0fdd1e98fbbdc12ba8d800aea360a64ad1c7"} {"question" "q-162239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following diagrams shows all the $3$rd roots of unity?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5f3091f264237278f4b144b278a0fdd1e98fbbdc12ba8d800aea360a64ad1c7"} {"question" "q-162239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Geometrically, the $3$rd roots of unity have the following properties:\n\n- all of them lie on the unit circle centered in the origin,\n\n- one of the roots is $1,$ corresponding to the point $(1,0)$ on the complex plane,\n\n- the roots form an equilateral triangle (regular $3$-sided polygon).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/assets/c70d25ac3a5ddb2d6765ef8a22f5e9774c9be06dd909d7079c3a361157881bb5.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995561/state.json" "file_sha256" "b5f3091f264237278f4b144b278a0fdd1e98fbbdc12ba8d800aea360a64ad1c7"} {"question" "q-162239" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Devel